The '''Galaxies Opera House''' was an opera theater located in the [[Uscru District]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]].

==Description==
[[File:SquidLake-ROTS.png|thumb|left|250px|A performance of ''Squid Lake'' at the Galaxies Opera House]]
The Galaxies Opera House was located in the upper levels of the [[Uscru District]], overlooking the levels below it.<ref name="Ultimate SW" /> It had two, large arching entrances where [[speeder]]s could unload their passengers. Within the entrances, steps led to the inside corridors wrapped around the main theater performance arena that was circular with seating areas on all sides.<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> In the waning days of the [[Galactic Republic]], [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]] maintained a private viewing box which had a premier view of the performance arena.<ref name="Ultimate SW" /> As visiting the [[opera]] house was a chance for patrons to stand out from the crowd, they followed the philosophy that the more extravagant their clothing was the better, wearing luxurious [[cloak]]s, elaborate headdresses, bold prints, and form-fitting dresses.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

==History==
===Clone Wars===
{{Quote|Did you ever hear the Tragedy of Darth Plagueis the Wise?''"<br />"''No.''"<br />"''I thought not. It's not a story the Jedi would tell you. It's a Sith legend.|Sheev Palpatine and Anakin Skywalker|<ref name="Episode III" />}}
Shortly after the [[Battle of Coruscant]], the [[Mon Calamari]] play ''[[Squid Lake]]'' was performed at the Galaxies Opera House.<ref name="Ultimate SW" /> Chancellor Palpatine attended the performance when he invited [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] to join him. Palpatine, secretly the [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] Darth Sidious, told Skywalker the [[Tragedy of Darth Plagueis the Wise|tale]] of [[Darth Plagueis]] and his attempts to cheat death. The story and Palpatine's manipulations were a major step in bringing Skywalker closer to the [[dark side of the Force]]. In the box beside Palpatine,<ref name="Episode III" /> [[First Minister (Coruscant Ministry of Ingress)|First Minister]] [[Tannon Praji]] of the [[Coruscant Ministry of Ingress]]<ref name="Insider">{{InsiderCite|217|Pushing Boundaries}}</ref> sat with their own companions to watch the show.<ref name="Episode III" />

===New Republic Era===
{{Quote|The Amnesty Program saved my life. There are many of us that had no choice in working for the Empire, but now, the New Republic has given us a second chance.|Penn Pershing addressing a gaia in [[9 ABY]]|<ref name="Chapter 19" />}}
[[File:PershingSpeech-TM19.png|thumb|right|250px|Former Imperial scientist Penn Pershing's speech at the opera house]]
The Galaxies Opera House continued to operate into the era of the [[New Republic]], with some seeing it as a symbol that Coruscant might once more rise again.<ref name="Galactic Explorer's Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]''</ref>

During [[9 ABY]], [[Doctor|Dr.]] [[Penn Pershing]] gave a speech in the Galaxies Opera House talking about his previous research into [[cloning]] and his recent acceptance into the [[New Republic Amnesty Program|Amnesty Program]] and expressed his willingness to help the New Republic.<ref name="Chapter 19">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 19: The Convert}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|I got to play that great scene — and one of the best scenes I think George has written. I know he's often teased about his writing, but he surpassed himself in the scene at the opera...When the old monster finally nails it with Anakin and gets him over to the Dark Side|Ian McDiarmid on the Galaxies Opera House scene|<ref name="ComicBook.com">{{WebCite|url=https://comicbook.com/starwars/2018/09/09/star-wars-revenge-of-the-sith-more-gruesome-order-66-scene-ian-mcdiarmid|text='Star Wars: Revenge of the Sith' Cut Down a "More Gruesome" Order 66 Scene|author=Bonomolo, Cameron|date=2018-09-09|work=ComicBook.com|archivedate=20190620064412}}</ref>}}
The Galaxies Opera House first appeared in the [[2005]] film [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']].<ref name="Episode III" /> [[Ian McDiarmid]] stated that the Galaxies Opera House scene was one of his favorite scenes of the saga and one of the best scenes [[George Lucas]] had ever written in his opinion.<ref name="ComicBook.com" />

